  "contracts": [
    "Each selected point expands to its own row; preserve repeated vertices and parent/point order independent of grouped reads.",
    "Float32-relative PointRoi normalization, rounded sampling and original subpixel world coordinates are distinct. Native SpatialCalibration affine defines world coordinates.",
    "Area is zero after single-pixel statistics; integrated density retains sampled physical pixel area times mean. Outside-image points retain original dtype-specific empty statistics and zero-sized bounds. Point diameter does not turn Analyzer points into area masks.",
    "Expanded row/record/kernel/retained-result and repeated ROI-name memory admission precedes provider reads; no full-plane point mask or repeated source scan.",
    "Selected manager API accepts nonempty bounded unique indices with optional document/metadata guards. Default absent indices means all; preserve explicit API order. UI Ctrl selection uses ascending stored row order.",
    "Point index is zero-based within its parent selection, not an ImageJ counter ID or counter population. T/C/Z comes from the frozen parent row/view until per-point annotation adapters land.",
    "Point diagnostics use version5 with frozen coordinates and point policy; earlier record meanings remain unchanged. Records are not replay instructions.",
    "Selected requests on unsupported RGB storage refuse explicitly; the actual selected-row control is disabled. Never fall through to legacy measure-all for the new indices/guards payload."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "M2b still requires per-point counters/positions and remaining required manager MultiMeasure/Z/T variants; parent-positioned points are scoped support.",
    "M3 area/shape/threshold/redirect/options, M4 reconciliation and T04a.3 session persistence/recorder/replay remain open.",
    "Finite scalar UInt8/UInt16/Float32; no RGB/IEEE/broad measurement-family completion.",
    "Actual UI qualified on Windows only; no Linux/macOS UI or release/ABI compatibility claim.",
    "No matched processing-speed superiority claim; storage remains unverified with inaccessible subtrees."
  ],
  "waste_review": {
    "fixed": [
      "Reuse one grouped source validation/table, existing 1x1 statistics instead of full-plane mask per point, existing jobs/formatter/row leases.",
      "Preflight expanded output count and charge repeated ROI names for every expanded row.",
      "Extend maintained observer/probe/capture route instead of new CLI/controller/runner.",
      "Physical manager-row reveal uses actual clip rectangle and verifies scroll progress; repeated ineffective coordinate clicks were not accepted.",
      "Final domain review guards selected-row dispatch against unsupported legacy fallback; installed core clients unchanged and their green evidence reused for this frontend-only fix."
    ],
    "failure_diagnostics": [
